%S A401018 0,0,1,0,1,1,1,0,2,1,1,1,1,1,2,0,2,2,2,1,4,1,1,1,1,1,4,1,2,2,2,0,3,2,
%T A401018 2,2,2,2,5,1,4,4,4,1,6,1,1,1,1,1,6,1,4,4,4,1,5,2,2,2,2,2,3,0,3,3,3,2,
%U A401018 7,2,2,2,2,2,9,2,5,5,5,1,7,4,4,4,4,4,9,1,6,6,6,1,8,1,1,1,1,1,8,1
%N A401018 Half the number of changes in the cyclic column words of the Gosper-Lafitte triangle.
%C A401018 Take the filled-empty word V(n)={v_0, v_1, ... , v_{q-1}} of length q=A002487(n+1) in column n of the fractal set described in A000360, read from the narrow top downward as in A400888. Put v_q = v_0 and dV(n,j) = v_j XOR v_{j+1}. We then consider the sequence a(n), where 2*a(n)= Sum_{j=0..q-1} dV(n,j). Thus 2*a(n) is the number of changes between consecutive digits in the cyclic word. Here a 0 -> 1 transition is indistinguishable from a 1 -> 0 transition, so a(n) counts either kind.
%C A401018 Equivalently, 2*a(n) is the Hamming weight of the cyclic first difference dV(n) over F_2.
%C A401018 Reversing, cyclic shifting or complementing V(n) keeps a(n) invariant. It is thus independent of both the reading direction of the column and the assignment of 0 and 1 to its two types of medial down-triangles.
%C A401018 The ranks 0<=n<3*2^r correspond to the columns from the left extremity to the central axis of the triangle at dyadic refinement level r, where the profile is the initial half of the level-(r+1) profile.
%C A401018 Every positive integer occurs; see the last formula.
%D A401018 M. Jeremie Lafitte (Levitas), Sur l'Effet Noah en Géométrie, rapport à l'INPI, Mars 1995.
%F A401018 Put p=A002487(n), q=A002487(n+1), and t = p mod q. Then 2*a(n) = {q when even, t when even and q odd, q-t when both q and t odd}.
%F A401018 a(2*n+1)=a(n), and a(2*n)= A002487(2*n + (n mod 3))/2, for n>=0.
%F A401018 Over the columns at dyadic refinement level r, Sum_{k=0..3*2^r-1} a(k) = Sum_{k=2^r..2^(r+1)-1} A002487(k) = 3^r, for r>=0.
%F A401018 a(2^(2*m-1)) = A002487(2^(2*m-1)+1)/2 = m, for m>=1.
%e A401018 V(18)={1,0,1,1,0,0,1}. Read cyclically, its boundary is dV(18)={1,1,0,1,0,1,0} which contains four 1s. Hence a(18) = 4/2 = 2. Also, p=A002487(18)=4, q=A002487(19)=7, t=4 mod 7=4, so the first formula gives 2*a(18)=t=4.
%e A401018 At level r=2, Sum_{k=0..11} a(k) = 0+0+1+0+1+1+1+0+2+1+1+1 = 9, while Sum_{k=4..7} A002487(k) = 1+3+2+3 = 9 = 3^2, illustrating the third formula.
%o A401018 (PARI)
%o A401018 s(n)=if(n<2,n,if(n%2,s(n\2)+s(n\2+1),s(n\2)));
%o A401018 a(n)={my(p=s(n),q=s(n+1),t=p%q); if(q%2==0,q/2,if(t%2==0,t/2,(q-t)/2))};
%o A401018 vector(100,n,a(n-1))
%o A401018 (Python)
%o A401018 from functools import reduce
%o A401018 def A002487(n): return 0 if n == 0 else sum(reduce(lambda x,y:(x[0],x[0]+x[1]) if int(y) else (x[0]+x[1],x[1]),bin(n)[-1:2:-1],(1,0)))
%o A401018 def A401018(n):
%o A401018     p, q = A002487(n), A002487(n+1)
%o A401018     t = p%q
%o A401018     if not q&1: return q>>1
%o A401018     if not t&1: return t>>1
%o A401018     return q-t>>1 # _Chai Wah Wu_, Oct 27 2026
%Y A401018 Cf. A000360 for the geometry, A000361 for the binary encodings, A400888.
%K A401018 nonn,eigen,new
%O A401018 0,9
%A A401018 _M. Jeremie Lafitte (Levitas)_, Oct 13 2026
